  "note": "Keys, note values and the single-note compass follow the RSL (Rockschool) Ukulele syllabus 2020 sight-reading parameters (official; Debut to Grade 5) with the London College of Music Ukulele 2023 syllabus as a cross-check for time signatures. Grade 0 = RSL Debut. RSL states a compass only for Debut, Grade 1 and Grade 2; from Grade 3 the profile uses the physical range of a soprano or concert ukulele (C4 to about A5, the lowest string is C4). Chord shapes and strumming are a human matter and are not measured: chord symbols are not read, so write the chords as symbols and the melody as notes. Tempo ceilings are our reading of the sight-reading and technical tempi. Standard GCEA re-entrant tuning, written at sounding pitch in treble clef. See references/instruments/ukulele.md.",
